  "body": "## A04 Linux userland compatibility baseline\n\nThis draft PR records reproducible original-Linux behavior, a fixed rootfs/workload contract, fixed-commit Hepta build evidence, and a guarded Asterinas differential entry point. It does not claim new-kernel compatibility or authenticated Hepta W1 completion.\n\n### Fixed inputs\n\n- Branch: `agents/A04-linux-hepta-baseline`\n- Current head: `77edc6bfe0ca7770d9433fb9b4fd98e3a463ff78`\n- Asterinas v0.19.0: `c4b7ed575b7b32773475b194d2ad41fb8d9345`\n- Hepta source: `f8c9419df6ddeb36ff8b522a50219981fb8d9345` (read-only)\n- Rootfs manifest SHA-256: `55aa8369d4f912267139ef7626c752814d7dc833e49accc337529f2545fb94cb`\n- Reviewed 17-file USTAR SHA-256: `df8df2e3cdcd308ef62a59268a4519e2923c9ff78145e46f26a4092725e80797`\n- Workload catalog SHA-256: `64b268956848d4fd97c6ace51343d607f20495d7bd317491a5bf7ead5e672db0` (32 cases: 28 ELF, 3 Python, 1 Rust/Tokio)\n\n### Verified original-Linux behavior\n\n- Current workload unit suite: 87 tests pass with 6 explicit managed-host skips, under both normal Python and `python3 -O`.\n- Reference contract: 31/32 application cases pass; Rust/Tokio remains explicit `not_run`.\n- Fixed C ELF set: 28/28 staged-loader and chroot cases pass; five-round chroot stress is 90/90.\n- SQLite private-source recheck: locked `libsqlite3-sys` 0.37.0 amalgamation built without installing packages; static/dynamic SQLite WAL and Python WAL pass with 40 commits, crash exit 37, 41 rows after reopen, rollback, checkpoint 0 and integrity OK.\n- Tokio has a reviewed Cargo.lock and locked release ELF build; runtime is blocked by managed pathname AF_UNIX `EPERM`.\n\n### Hepta evidence\n\nThe fixed Hepta source built through the real `runtime_codex_product_e2e` path. The debug test ELF is `5c34f4ce5aca36ea2619e42aef2673c092641e0c888cda9b1147542e844414`; it is build evidence only and does not replace the release ELF hash pinned in `compat/linux/hepta-profile.json`. Loader and direct libraries are recorded in `tests/workloads/linux/baselines/hepta-cloud-probe-20261016.json`.\n\nThe e2e test exited 101 after Wiremock matched zero Responses requests; no provider request or terminal tool-effect receipt was produced. The fixed source search found the invocation-provider trait but zero concrete implementations and zero standalone attachment calls. `strace` is blocked by `PTRACE_TRACEME=EPERM`; the trace guard rejects the debug ELF against the release profile hash. These are host composition/provider/sandbox blockers, not kernel ABI evidence.\n\n### QEMU and host-policy blockers\n\nThe replay preflight verified the pinned A01 kernel/initramfs hashes and exited 2 with `blocked_environment_or_input` because QEMU/SeaBIOS are absent. No A04 workload has run under Asterinas/QEMU in this environment. Pathname and abstract AF_UNIX creation and ptrace are denied by the managed cloud policy (`Seccomp=2`, `NoNewPrivs=1`, `CapEff=0`); namespace/bwrap attempts did not change this. These cases require an authorized Linux/QEMU host before they can become guest results.\n\n### Scope and handoff\n\nAll A04-owned implementation/evidence paths are under `compat/linux/**`, `support/rootfs/**`, and `tests/workloads/linux/**`; the root `README.md` remains 0 bytes. Run `tests/workloads/linux/replay_qemu.py` with the pinned A01 artifacts and fixed rootfs, preserve serial/raw exit and exact facts, then use `compat/linux/compare.py`. Route an actual guest ABI mismatch to A05/A06 and the authenticated Agentd/provider composition gap to A07.",
